# PROFILE.example — instance values for this pipeline

Fill this in for your install. Each token below is referenced by the card
bodies in `cards/` and by the kickoff/handoff recipes in `board.md` /
`spec.md`. Substitute all six before running; leave the `__PIPELINE_INPUT__`
and `__CHANGESSET_MANIFEST__` tokens in place (they are substituted per run
by the creating card, not here).

## The tokens

- **`{{ASSIGNEE}}`** — the Hermes profile(s) that run the cards. This is
  the `--assignee` on every `kanban create`. It is **one token** that
  resolves per site (never split into per-role tokens):
    - **Single-runner install** — the value is one profile name; every
      card runs as that profile (it must have the house skill, the repo,
      and the kanban toolset). `ASSIGNEE = myprofile`
    - **Role-isolated install** — the value is a `role=profile` map; the
      assembler fills each `{{ASSIGNEE}}` site with the profile for the
      role of the card that site creates, read from the map. One profile
      + one Hindsight bank per role severs the shared-memory backchannel
      between adversarial roles (an Audit/Verifier must not recall what
      the Author/Scripter it is checking reasoned).
      `ASSIGNEE = author=sr-author, audit=sr-audit, ste100=sr-ste100,
      scripter=sr-scripter, verifier=sr-verifier, commit=sr-commit,
      fleet=sr-fleet`
  One pipeline per repo (R3) assumes one assignee's worktree. The kickoff
  records `--created-by` as the orchestrator's profile (who ran the
  `hermes kanban create`); that equals `{{ASSIGNEE}}` only in the
  single-runner case.

- **`{{REPO_DIR}}`** — absolute path to your house skill repo checkout.
  This is the `--workspace dir:` target on every card and the place the
  pipeline reads/writes skills, runs `tools/lint_skills.py`, and (only on
  the Commit card) commits + pushes. Must be a clean `git` checkout of a
  repo with a `CONVENTIONS.md` and `tools/lint_skills.py` at its root.

- **`{{CARDS_DIR}}`** — absolute directory holding the seven card bodies in
  `cards/`. Some cards' handoff step tells the successor to *read its own
  canonical body from disk* (instead of inlining it, to stay under the 8 KB
  body cap) — that read path is `{{CARDS_DIR}}/<sibling>.md`. Point this at
  wherever you install the `cards/` tree.

- **`{{MID_MODEL}}`** — the model id for the grunt-work cards: Author,
  Scripter, and the retry cards they spawn (the retry Author cards and the
  retry Scripter card carry an explicit `--model` pin; the STE100 retry
  Author does too). This is the *lower* tier — drafting and mechanical
  script-writing. The judgment cards (Audit, Verifier, Commit,
  Fleet-Update-Check, and the STE100 card itself) carry **no** `--model`,
  so they run on the operator's default (the *higher* tier). Pick a model
  id that your LLM proxy actually serves under that name. (Role-isolated
  install: a role that should run mid is given a profile whose default is
  mid — the pin travels with the profile, not the card.)

- **`{{HOUSE_SKILL}}`** — the name of the house-repo skill that documents
  how to work in `{{REPO_DIR}}` (the rubric, the linter, the commit
  discipline). It is force-loaded on every card except the STE100 card.
  Default: `hermes-skills-repo`.

- **`{{STD_SKILL}}`** — the name of the writing-standard skill (the
  ASD-STE100 controlled-language skill) force-loaded on the **STE100** card
  only. The STE100 card audits a draft against this standard and never
  restates it (the force-loaded SKILL.md is already in the worker's
  context). Default: `asd-ste100`.

## Worked example (what a filled PROFILE looks like)

Single-runner install (one profile runs every card):

```
ASSIGNEE     = myprofile
REPO_DIR     = <absolute>/hermes-skills
CARDS_DIR    = <absolute>/.hermes/profiles/myprofile/future-work/skill-kanban-cards
MID_MODEL    = <your-mid-tier-model-id>
HOUSE_SKILL  = hermes-skills-repo
STD_SKILL    = asd-ste100
```

Role-isolated install (one profile + one Hindsight bank per role; same
single `{{ASSIGNEE}}` token, value is the map):

```
ASSIGNEE     = author=sr-author, audit=sr-audit, ste100=sr-ste100,
               scripter=sr-scripter, verifier=sr-verifier,
               commit=sr-commit, fleet=sr-fleet
REPO_DIR     = <absolute>/hermes-skills
CARDS_DIR    = <absolute>/.hermes/profiles/<operator>/future-work/skill-kanban-cards
MID_MODEL    = <your-mid-tier-model-id>
HOUSE_SKILL  = hermes-skills-repo
STD_SKILL    = asd-ste100
```

Every `{{ASSIGNEE}}` in `cards/` resolves to the map entry for the role of
the card that site creates (e.g. the Author's "create the Audit" handoff
→ `audit=` → `sr-audit`).

## Notes

- `{{MID_MODEL}}` and the default (high) tier must both be resolvable by
  the same proxy with the same profile key, or the grunt cards will fall
  over at spawn.
- The model tiers are a *per-card-class* decision, not a per-run one: the
  split is "drafting/scripting = mid, judging/committing = high." Do not
  pin a judgment card to mid — that is where the bug-catch and the only
  push live.
- Keep the `cards/` bodies' `RULES IN FORCE` and handoff sections under the
  8 KB stored-body cap even after substitution (see `known-pitfalls.md`).
